  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 3 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of five years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 4 - 10.2\tThe proposed application provides for a use that contributes to public transport provision in the area and is considered to make best use of previously developed land, and mitigating for any adverse affect upon the amenities of adjoining residential properties. The proposal also provides satisfactory servicing arrangements. This is in accordance with policies IMP.1.2 (The Reuse and Recycling of Urban Land and Buildings), ENV.B.1.1 (New Development), T.1.4 (Car and Cycle Parking and Servicing of Development) of the adopted Unitary Development Plan 2003.",
    "Condition : 5 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 6 - The parking, loading and turning spaces shown on drawing No. B-nc-08 SK-1 shall be constructed and available for use before first occupation of any part of the development and such spaces shall not be used for any other purposes.",
    "Condition : 7 - The bus wash hereby approved shall not be operated between the hours 23.00 and 0600am, unless otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 8 - Prior to development commencing a management plan shall be submitted to and approved by the local planning authority, specifying the hours of operation and timing of the circulation of the buses around the site for a 24 hour period. The approved scheme shall be implemented in accordance with those details or as otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority.\r\n",
    "Condition : 9 - Under no circumstances shall the northern, eastern and southern areas of the service yard be used by buses between the hours of 22.00 and 07.00 unless otherwise agreed  in writing by the Local Planning Authority."
  ],
